  "wikipedia": {
    "title": "Zeta Canis Majoris",
    "description": "Binary star in the constellation Canis Major",
    "summary": "Zeta Canis Majoris is a binary star system in the southern constellation of Canis Major. Its name is a Bayer designation that is Latinized from ζ Canis Majoris; it has the proper name Furud, pronounced. This system has a combined apparent visual magnitude of +3.0, making it one of the brighter stars in the constellation and hence readily visible to the naked eye. Parallax measurements from the Hipparcos mission yield a distance estimate of around 362 ly (111 pc) from the Sun. It is drifting further away with a radial velocity of +32 km/s.",
    "intro": "Zeta Canis Majoris is a binary star system in the southern constellation of Canis Major. Its name is a Bayer designation that is Latinized from ζ Canis Majoris; it has the proper name Furud, pronounced . This system has a combined apparent visual magnitude of +3.0, making it one of the brighter stars in the constellation and hence readily visible to the naked eye. Parallax measurements from the Hipparcos mission yield a distance estimate of around 362 ly (111 pc) from the Sun. It is drifting further away with a radial velocity of +32 km/s.",
    "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zeta_Canis_Majoris",
